    "narrative": "Today\u2019s offensive outlook for the Austin Waves centers on the high-upside pairing of **Kyle Tucker** (80.25) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27). **Kyle Tucker** is our undisputed anchor, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Singer with a +14% boost from SP skill and an ideal #3 spot in the order. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** is a high-conviction start; despite the lineup being pending, he benefits from a massive +14% park adjustment and a +13% platoon edge against Gordon, making him an elite option for today\u2019s 5x5 needs. **Miguel Vargas** also warrants attention; while facing a veteran in Framber Valdez, **Miguel Vargas** retains a strong 59.81 score, buoyed by the potential for stolen bases against a pitcher with a traditionally slow delivery, which remains a critical KPI for our roster strategy.\n\nManaging our remaining utility spots required a delicate touch. **Josh Jung** (50.01) and **Sam Antonacci** (49.14) represent our most precarious starts. **Sam Antonacci** was a candidate for the bench due to his L/L platoon disadvantage against Valdez, but his projected role keeps him in the mix. The most difficult \"sit\" decision involved **Wade Meckler** (47.45); he barely edged out our depth options thanks to a late-breaking +5% wind-out factor and his favorable spot in the order, narrowly justifying his inclusion over the lower-tier floor players on our bench. **Liam Hicks** (43.94) rounds out the active roster, though his value is capped today by a negative park adjustment and a difficult platoon matchup against Springs, leaving him in the marginal category.\n\nRisk management remains a primary concern as we head into the evening. With several lineups\u2014specifically **Miguel Vargas**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Josh Jung**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Wade Meckler**\u2014still pending, we are exposed to potential late-scratch volatility. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Andy Pages**, who remain on the IL, alongside our dormant studs **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who are inactive today. The focus for the rest of the roster remains on maintaining our SB ceiling, necessitating that we keep a close watch on the defensive alignments to ensure our high-sprint-speed options maintain their projected order advantages.",
